summary:
Rekaind Vertical Services, Inc. is an independent elevator and escalator maintenance contractor headquartered in Philadelphia. It licenses the LiftSense remote-monitoring and predictive-maintenance platform from Velert Systems, LLC of Columbus, Ohio, under a Software License Agreement effective March 3, 2025. The folder holds the license, its Service Level Schedule, the Order Form for 1,140 units, a May 2025 side letter, Rekaind's October 21, 2026 notice of termination for chronic availability failure, and two distractors (Rekaind's dispatch-center office lease and Velert's certificate of insurance). Six issues are planted:
- an exclusivity covenant that reaches all equipment Rekaind or its affiliates service worldwide;
- a one-sided Velert assignment right;
- a side letter that restructures the indemnity so that bodily-injury indemnity falls under the cap;
- an Order Form choosing Ohio law and forum that controls through the precedence clause;
- a 36-month auto-renewal with a 15-day opt-out window;
- a chronic-failure termination notice sent after the Service Level Schedule's 30-day exercise window closed.
